#* {{quote-book|en|year=1833|author=[[w:Samuel Hahnemann|S{{quote-gloss|amuel}} Hahnemann]]|chapter_tlr=Charles H. Devrient|chapter=Organon of Medicine|title=[[w:The Organon of the Healing Art|The Homœopathic Medical Doctrine, or, “Organon of the Healing Art;” a New System of Physic,]]{{nb...|Translated from the German of S. Hahnemann, by Charles H. Devrient, Esq., with Notes by Samuel Stratten, M.&nbsp;D.}}|location=Dublin|publisher=W{{quote-gloss|illiam}} F{{quote-gloss|rederick}} Wakeman,{{nb...|9, D’Olier-St.}}; London: [[w:Simpkin & Marshall|Simpkin and Marshall]] and R{{quote-gloss|ichard}} Groombridge; Edinburgh: Maclachlan and Stewart|section=§ LVIII|page=154|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/bub_gb_EnEFAAAAQAAJ/page/n182/mode/1up|oclc=3254663|passage=The source of all these pernicious results of palliative '''antipathic''' treatment, and the salutary effects proceeding from the reverse method, the homœopathic, will be sufficiently explained in the following observations which are drawn from experience and a number of facts that have hitherto escaped the notice of every one save myself, although they were immediately before the view, perfectly evident in their nature, and of the deepest importance to the medical art.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1906|month=October|title=Homeopathy vs. Anti-pathy|editor=H{{quote-gloss|enry}} C{{quote-gloss|lay}} Allen|journal=The Medical Advance and Journal of Homeopathics|volume=XLIV|issue=10|location=Batavia, Ill.|publisher=J{{quote-gloss|ames}} E. Forrest|section=Department of Homeopathics (conducted by Guernsey P{{quote-gloss|enny}} Waring)|page=648|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/themedicaladvanceandjournalofhomeopathicsamonthlyjournalofhahnemannianhomeopathy3444.1906/page/n709/mode/1up|oclc=245506160|passage=This sham and duplicity cannot be longer excused or tolerated. Those who recommend and bodily use '''antipathic''' methods should announce themselves as allopaths and train with that school of practice, and no longer misrepresent and dishonor the homeopathic system.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|author=w:Andrew Weil|chapter=Like Cures Like, and Less Is More|title=Health and Healing: Understanding Conventional and Alternative Medicine|location=Boston, Mass.|publisher=[[w:Houghton Mifflin Harcourt|Houghton Mifflin Company]]|section=part I (Treatment and Cure: The Strange Case of Homeopathy)|page=17|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/healthhealingund00weil/page/17/mode/1up|isbn=0-395-34430-1|passage=The opposite of treatment by similars is treatment by contraries, and Hahnemann called this practice antipathy. Giving aspirin to lower fever or prescribing antihypertensive drugs to treat high blood pressure are examples of '''antipathic''' medicine.}}

